  ],
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "5e87feff-d1a1-47f1-aa35-eb9dc3dee7f3",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        -520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Day 81 Solution: Managing Clients with Automation\n\nTwo real workflows on this canvas:\n\n**1) Support Triage** (Webhook trigger, left column) \u2014 classifies an inbound client message with OpenAI, routes FAQ questions to an automated reply, and escalates billing/technical/feature-request/uncertain messages to Slack for a human.\n\n**2) Weekly Client Report** (Schedule Trigger, right column) \u2014 pulls real execution data from the n8n Executions API, computes success rate with a Code node, asks OpenAI for one written observation, and sends the report over Slack.\n\n**Credentials needed to run this for real:** OpenAI API key; Gmail (or Slack) for the FAQ auto-reply; Slack API for escalations and the weekly report; an n8n API key for the Executions API call (replace the placeholder base URL/header value with your own).\n\n**Matches:** `DAILY_TASKS/DAY_81_Managing_Clients_Automation.md`",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 480
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d58362e0-4c83-4a4c-a4eb-5556d272e107",
      "name": "FAQ Content Reference",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        -60
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Real FAQ Content (used verbatim in the Draft FAQ Reply system prompt)\n\n**Q: How do I access my dashboard?**\nA: Go to app.lane-automation.example, sign in with your account email, and your dashboard loads on the Overview tab.\n\n**Q: How do I pause or resume a workflow?**\nA: Open the workflow, use the Active toggle in the top-right corner. Pausing does not delete history or executions.\n\n**Q: How do I change which email/Slack channel gets my alerts?**\nA: Settings -> Notifications -> update the destination, then Save. Changes apply to the next run.\n\n**Q: How do I read my weekly report?**\nA: 'Success rate' is the % of runs that completed without error; 'executions' is total runs; the note at the bottom flags anything unusual that week.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 480
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f31d23b4-4e73-4c7f-a23c-e3b301d22e15",
      "name": "Client Support Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -200,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "path": "client-support",
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7879aba5-bc19-45cd-8e9e-2de46f757061",
      "name": "Classify Message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        40,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "chat",
        "operation": "create",
        "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You classify inbound client support messages for an automation agency. Reply with exactly one word, lowercase, no punctuation: faq, billing, technical_issue, or feature_request. Use 'faq' only for questions matching these known topics: accessing the dashboard, pausing/resuming a workflow, changing notification destinations, or reading the weekly report. Anything about invoices, charges, or payment is 'billing'. Anything about a workflow erroring, failing, or behaving unexpectedly is 'technical_issue'. Requests for new capabilities are 'feature_request'. If truly unsure, reply 'uncertain'."
            },
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "={{ 'Subject: ' + $json.subject + '\\n\\nBody: ' + $json.body }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.1,
          "maxTokens": 10
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "82a8380a-3ecb-49a8-8b41-fe3f81b35a7d",
      "name": "Parse Category",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        280,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const valid = ['faq', 'billing', 'technical_issue', 'feature_request'];\nconst raw = (item.json.message && item.json.message.content ? item.json.message.content : '')\n  .toString().trim().toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z_]/g, '');\nconst category = valid.includes(raw) ? raw : 'uncertain';\nreturn { json: { ...($('Client Support Webhook').item.json), category } };"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "41b57e6e-918b-4f0b-8bbf-92f3b5af7c3c",
      "name": "Route by Category",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch",
      "typeVersion": 3.2,
      "position": [
        520,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "rules",
        "rules": {
          "values": [
            {
              "conditions": {
                "string": [
                  {
                    "value1": "={{ $json.category }}",
                    "operation": "equals",
                    "value2": "faq"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "outputKey": "faq"
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "string": [
                  {
                    "value1": "={{ $json.category }}",
                    "operation": "equals",
                    "value2": "billing"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "outputKey": "billing"
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "string": [
                  {
                    "value1": "={{ $json.category }}",
                    "operation": "equals",
                    "value2": "technical_issue"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "outputKey": "technical_issue"
            },
            {
              "conditions": {
                "string": [
                  {
                    "value1": "={{ $json.category }}",
                    "operation": "equals",
                    "value2": "feature_request"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "outputKey": "feature_request"
            }
          ]
        },
        "fallbackOutput": "extra"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "14ccc2db-75b6-4b7f-964d-29ee9589d7a2",
      "name": "Draft FAQ Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        800,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "chat",
        "operation": "create",
        "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You are the support auto-reply for an automation agency. Answer ONLY using this real FAQ content, in a friendly 2-4 sentence reply. Dashboard access: go to app.lane-automation.example, sign in with your account email, dashboard loads on the Overview tab. Pause/resume a workflow: open the workflow, use the Active toggle top-right; pausing keeps history. Change alert destination: Settings -> Notifications -> update destination -> Save. Reading the weekly report: success rate is % of error-free runs, executions is total runs, the bottom note flags anything unusual. If the question doesn't match these topics, say you'll have a teammate follow up instead of guessing."
            },
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "={{ $json.subject + ': ' + $json.body }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.3,
          "maxTokens": 300
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "90deda8c-ddbb-4bc5-aef2-7dfc670a1056",
      "name": "Send FAQ Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        1040,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "message",
        "operation": "send",
        "sendTo": "={{ $('Route by Category').item.json.from }}",
        "subject": "={{ 'Re: ' + $('Route by Category').item.json.subject }}",
        "message": "={{ $json.message.content }}",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
